      "hints": [
        "Gradient of $AB$ is $\\frac{3}{4} \\implies$ perpendicular gradient $-\\frac{4}{3}$.",
        "Equation of $BC$: $y - 4 = -\\frac{4}{3}(x - 3) \\implies y = -\\frac{4}{3}x + 8$.",
        "Set $y = 0$ to find $x_C = 6$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Calculate the gradient of $AB$ through $A(-1, 1)$ and $B(3, 4)$:\n$$m_{AB} = \\frac{4 - 1}{3 - (-1)} = \\frac{3}{4}$$",
        "Determine the perpendicular gradient for $BC$:\n$$m_{BC} = -\\frac{1}{3/4} = -\\frac{4}{3}$$",
        "Write the equation of the line $BC$ passing through $B(3, 4)$:\n$$y - 4 = -\\frac{4}{3}(x - 3) \\implies y = -\\frac{4}{3}x + 4 + 4 \\implies y = -\\frac{4}{3}x + 8$$",
        "Find the $x$-coordinate of $C$ by setting $y = 0$:\n$$-\\frac{4}{3}x + 8 = 0 \\implies \\frac{4}{3}x = 8 \\implies x = 8 \\times \\frac{3}{4} = 6$$"
      ],
